  "result": "The bug is fixed and the tests pass. `python3 -m shop quote a:12.5:2` now prints 27.06 (run via the `-c` fallback, since there is no `__main__.py`).\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded the fractional part with `rjust`, which pads on the left. `\"5\"` became `\"05\"`, so `12.5` parsed as 12.05 instead of 12.50. The quote came out as 26.09 instead of 27.06.\n\n**Fix:** `shop/money.py:9` now uses `ljust(2, \"0\")`.\n\n**Tests:** `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` ran 12 tests, all OK. That is the 6 existing tests plus 6 new ones in `tests/test_money.py`. The new tests cover `to_cents` for `12.5`, `12.05`, `12.50`, `12`, and `0.9`, plus a CLI check that `quote a:12.5:2` prints `27.06`. The existing suite passed before the fix too, because nothing tested a one-digit fraction. I did not open the new test file myself after the worker wrote it. The results above are from the worker's run.\n\n**Notes:**\n- pytest isn't installed, so I used unittest, which the README specifies.\n- `python3 -m shop` still fails because the package has no `__main__.py`. I left that alone; say if you want it added.\n- Nothing is committed.",
